    "original_review_scope_verbatim": "Complete original Theorem1.1 and both finite-regularity and smooth-metric path-connectivity arguments. The exact KO-index lower bound, quaternionic kernel dimension, spin structure, closed/connected/dimension hypotheses, all C-ell and C-infinity topologies, conformally-flat exceptional subset and codimension conventions are retained. The full actual new harmonic-spinor deformation, energy-momentum/gradient identity, rank-two transversality, Banach-submersion/codimension proof, infinite-codimension exceptional-set proof and connectedness lemma are retained. These intermediate statements are necessary core, not extra counts. Unrelated introductory surgery/genus/minimal-surface examples are excluded, while original Remarks1.2 items4–6 on regularity and flatness retain their source numbering via an editorial list wrapper. Three unused lowercase-counter theorem environment declarations from the publisher class are omitted; none occurs in selected text. All used author macros and proof formulas are unchanged. Standard index theory, spinor-bundle variation, elliptic regularity, unique continuation and Banach-space prerequisites remain exact author references.\n\nNo mathematical refereeing or assistant-generated proof. Native source and corresponding saved publisher PDF are hash-bound. The required two fresh no-shell-escape XeLaTeX passes exit0. Final log has no undefined references, missing characters, overfull boxes, font substitutions or label-rerun warning. Every retained original source block occurs byte-for-byte exactly once in the editable standalone TeX. Original archive entry/source/PDF versions are hash-bound and directly verified. Actual source/output formulas were compared as follows.\n\n\nOriginal journal main statement PDF3/output2, energy-momentum gradient and rank-two proof PDF14–15/output12–13, and complete finite/smooth connectivity proof PDF17/output15 compared. Quaternionic double angles, chiral Dirac labels, dimension2/4 cases, exceptional conformally flat metrics and the smooth approximation paragraph are all retained. Only unused lowercase-counter environment declarations are omitted from the standalone preamble; all selected formulas/macros remain literal. Original Remarks1.2 regularity/flatness items4–6 retain the source numbering; excluded items1–3 are unrelated examples.\n\n\nCompiler-only immutable revision r002: original announced r001 files remain unchanged. Exact TeX, author excerpts, metadata, license facts, source maps and assets retain their original bytes. A fresh 3-pass no-shell-escape compilation stabilizes both auxiliary and outline files; final log has no label/outline/bookmark rerun, multiply-defined-label, missing-glyph, overfull or undefined warning. No mathematical or body edit. Every page of the original announced PDF and the repaired PDF is pixel-identical under matching72dpi PyMuPDF rendering, recorded in visual-qa.json. Visible author mathematics/text/layout do not change; only compiler/outline qualification is repaired.\n",
